@ 6.2.2.1.9 - Classical Arabic to Wādı̄ Hadhrami Arabic
# citation: Pogostick Man, from Wikipedia Contributors (2013), “Hadhrami Arabic”. Wikipedia, the Free Encyclopedia. Epenthesis (it seems i is preferred) breaking up final consonant clusters
	d͡ʒ > j, occasionally ɟ or d͡ʒ in educated speech
	{ θ, ð, ðˤ } > { t, d, dˤ }
	{ dˤ, q } > { ðˤ, ɡ }
	a:[+long] > e:[+long]
	a:[+long] > æ:[+long]
	V:[-long] > ∅ / #C_C (sporadic?)